(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-08-23"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-08-23","label":"2026 年 8 月 23 日","date":"2026-08-23","range":"","theme":"科技","themes":["科技"],"sources":["Economist"],"title":"Well Informed","titleZh":"心里有数——健康专栏","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":8,"vocab":42,"question":15,"qa":0,"original":4,"layout":1},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"8.23 精读.pdf","headline":{"title":"Well Informed","titleZh":"心里有数——健康专栏","source":"Economist","series":"考研那些事儿之科技系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"The trillions of bugs in a human gut digest complex carbohydrates into fatty acids that provide about 10% of an individual’s calories. They synthesise vitamins, notably K (which regulates blood clotting) and various members of the B group. They help tune the immune system. They suppress the growth of pathogens. And they regulate production of signalling molecules, such as serotonin, involved in sending messages from the gut to the brain.","zh":"人体肠道中数以万亿计的微生物会将复杂碳水化合物消化分解成脂肪酸，为人体提供约10%的热量。它们还能合成维生素，尤其是维生素K（能够调节血液凝固）以及多种B族维生素；帮助调节免疫系统；抑制病原体的生长；并调控血清素等信号分子的生成，向大脑传递肠道信息也有这些信号分子的功劳。"},{"index":2,"en":"Keeping your gut microbiome in tip-top condition is thus wise. Maintaining a diverse mix of bacteria in it is widely thought a good way to do this. And, since different species have different appetites, diversity of diet makes sense.","zh":"因此，保持肠道微生物组处于最佳状态实属明智之举。人们普遍认为，维持肠道内菌群多样化有助于保证微生物群的良好状态。而且，由于不同菌种的口味各不相同，饮食种类丰富也十分重要。"},{"index":3,"en":"In 2018 an American citizen-science project showed that people eating 30 types of plants a week had significantly more diverse microbiomes than those eating fewer than ten. And work from Stanford University, published in 2021, confirmed that fermented foods such as kimchi and sauerkraut diversify microbiomes, too. Some people, though, feel such off-the-peg advice is insufficient. They would prefer something bespoke.","zh":"2018年，一项由美国公众参与的科学研究项目显示，每周食用30种植物食物的人，其肠道微生物组多样性明显高于每周食用不足10种的人。斯坦福大学2021年发表的一项研究也证实，泡菜、酸菜等发酵食品同样能够增加肠道微生物组的多样性。不过，有些人觉得这种一刀切式的建议还不够。他们更希望得到量身定制的方案。"},{"index":4,"en":"For a suitable fistful of dollars, they can have it. So-called direct-to- consumer (D2C) firms will analyse stool samples and compile lists of the bugs therein, based on the DNA and RNA they find. Such firms may also offer tailored dietary recommendations, doses of live bacteria and special bug-friendly supplements, all intended to fill any microbial blanks that their tests have flagged up.","zh":"只要花上一笔钱，他们就能得到这样的服务。所谓直接面向消费者（D2C）的公司会分析粪便样本，根据其中检测到的DNA和RNA，列出样本中所含微生物的清单。这类公司可能还会提供个性化的饮食建议、活菌剂量以及专门有利于微生物生长的补充剂，旨在填补检测所发现的微生物缺失。"},{"index":5,"en":"The problem with this approach is that there is no \"right\" microbiome to act as a reference. In fact, microbiomes can differ quite a bit from each other while still being perfectly effective at delivering a desirable outcome to their host. The biggest red flag for poor gut health is a simple lack of biodiversity—which is what a varied and partly fermented diet is good at correcting. By contrast, the idea that tinkering with the presence or absence of this or that type of bug will perceptibly improve your health has scant published scientific basis, and many D2C firms are reluctant to share the details of proprietary data on which they base their claims.","zh":"这种方法的问题在于，可以作为参照标准的所谓“正确”微生物组并不存在。事实上，不同人体内的微生物组可能存在相当大的差异，却依然能够非常有效地为宿主带来理想的结果。肠道健康不佳最明显的警讯，是生物多样性不足，而多样化、且部分经过发酵的饮食恰恰有助于纠正这一问题。相比之下，认为通过调整某一种微生物的存在与否，就能让健康状况得到明显改善，这一观点几乎没有什么已发表的科学依据；而且，许多D2C公司也不愿公开其相关主张所依据的专有数据的具体细节。"},{"index":6,"en":"There are exceptions. In Britain, Tim Spector has ridden the twin horses of academic science (a post at King’s College, London) and commerce (he helped found a D2C firm called Zoe) without so far falling off. Results from Zoe’s customers are fed, with their permission, into respectable, peer-reviewed research. So far, this suggests individually tailored diets do not have huge effects, but may help at the margins.","zh":"当然，也有例外。在英国，蒂姆·斯佩克特（TimSpector）横跨学商两界，他在伦敦国王学院任职的同时，还参与创办了一家名为Zoe的D2C公司。到目前为止，他在两个身份之间来回切换，游刃有余。经客户许可，Zoe公司收集到的用户数据会被纳入正规的同行评议研究。截至目前，这些研究表明，个性化饮食并不会产生特别显著的效果，但或许能在一些细微之处有所帮助。"},{"index":7,"en":"However, even if a bespoke approach does have value, it must surely depend on the microbial censuses carried out by D2C firms being accurate. To test that, researchers at America’s National Institute of Standards and Technology prepared 21 sets of homogenised (and thus identical) faeces and sent three to each of seven D2C firms. When the results (which were published in February) came back there were notable differences not only between different firms’ analyses but also, in one case, between those of an individual company.","zh":"不过，即便量身定制的方法确实有价值，它显然也必须建立在D2C公司所进行的微生物普查足够准确的基础上。为了检验这一点，美国国家标准与技术研究院的研究人员制备了21份经过均质处理、因而完全相同的粪便样本，并给向7家D2C公司每家寄出了3份。检测结果（已于2月发表）寄回后，人们发现，不仅不同公司的分析结果之间存在明显差异，甚至有一家公司的检测结果内部也有不同。"},{"index":8,"en":"As Jonathan Eisen, an evolutionary microbiologist at the University of California, Davis, observes, just because microbiomes differ does not mean an era of personalised microbiome medicine is coming any time soon. In fact, he puts it more strongly than this, saying, \"Most of the claims [in this area] are bogus.\" Perhaps better to save your money and invest in a jar of kimchi.","zh":"加州大学戴维斯分校的进化微生物学家乔纳森·艾森（JonathanEisen）指出，微生物组存在差异，并不意味着个性化微生物组医学时代就会很快到来。其实，他本人的话更为直接：“（这个领域的）大多数说法都是骗人的。”所以，你也许还是省下这笔钱，买罐泡菜更好。"}],"vocab":[{"term":"hack","head":"v. /hæk/ to find a way of looking at and/or changing","definition":"information on sb else's computer system without","gloss":"permission非法侵入（他人的计算机系统）；黑客攻击【考研","example":"The bank's security system was hacked by a group of","exampleZh":"大纲词汇】 cybercriminals.该银行的安全系统遭到一群网络罪犯的非法侵 入。","tags":[]},{"term":"gut","head":"n. /ɡʌt/ the tube in the body through which food","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"passes when it leaves the stomach 消化道；肠道【考研大纲","exampleZh":"词汇】 The bacteria in your gut play a crucial role in digestion. 你 肠道中的细菌在消化过程中起着至关重要的作用。","tags":[]},{"term":"guts","head":"n. /ɡʌts/ (informal) the courage and determination","definition":"","gloss":"that it takes to do sth difficult or unpleasant 勇气；胆量；","example":"He doesn't have the guts to walk away from a well-paid","exampleZh":"决心；毅力 job.他没胆量辞去一份报酬优厚的工作。","tags":[]},{"term":"microbiome","head":"n. /ˌmaɪkrəʊˈbaɪəʊm/ the community of","definition":"microorganisms (such as bacteria, fungi, and viruses) that live in a particular environment, especially in the human","gloss":"body微生物组；微生物群落","example":"The human microbiome is of particular interest, as these commensal bacteria are important for human health and","exampleZh":"immunity.人类微生物组尤其令人关注，因为这些共生细菌对人 类健康和免疫力至关重要。","tags":[]},{"term":"bug","head":"n. /b ʌ ɡ / (informal) an illness that is usually not","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"serious and is caused by bacteria or a virus （引起小毛病","exampleZh":"的）细菌；病毒【考研大纲词汇】 I had a tummy/stomach bug last week. 上周我的肠胃出了点 小毛病。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"carbohydrate","head":"n. /ˌkɑːbəʊˈhaɪdreɪt/ a substance such as","definition":"sugar or starch that consists of carbon, hydrogen and oxygen. Carbohydrates in food provide the body with","gloss":"","example":"energyandheat.碳水化合物；糖类【考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"Nuts are high in carbohydrates. 坚果富含碳水化合物。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"synthesise","head":"v. /ˈsɪnθəsaɪz/ (also synthesize) to produce a","definition":"","gloss":"substance by a chemical reaction in plants or animals 合成","example":"There are many vitamins that the body cannot synthesize ANT break down","exampleZh":"【考研大纲词汇】 itself.有很多维生素是人体自身无法合成的。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"clot","head":"v. /klɒt/ when blood or cream clots or when sth clots","definition":"","gloss":"it, it forms thick, almost solid masses （血液或奶油）凝结成","example":"He was rushed into hospital because his blood wasn't","exampleZh":"块；使凝结【考研大纲词汇】 clottingproperly.他被匆忙送进医院，因为他的血液不能正常 凝结。 n. an almost solid piece of something 凝块 He had a blood clot removed from his brain. 他颅内的一个 血块被取了出来。 n. a stupid person 傻瓜，笨蛋 Look what you've done, you clot! 看看你干了什么，笨蛋！","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"tune","head":"v. /tjuːn/ to prepare or change sth so that it is","definition":"","gloss":"suitable for a particular situation 调整；使适合；使协调【考","example":"His speech was tuned to what the audience wanted to be in/out of tune with someone/something idiomif you are in tune with people or ideas, you understand or agree with them, and if you are out of tune with them, you do Much of his success comes from being in tune with what Her theories were out of tune with the scientific thinking","exampleZh":"研大纲词汇】 hear.他的演讲根据听众的期望进行了调整。 not.与…协调／不协调，与…相／不相契合 hiscustomerswant.他的成功很大程度上归功于他契合了顾客 的需要。 ofthetime.她的理论与当时的科学思想不符。","tags":[]},{"term":"suppress","head":"v. /səˈpres/ to prevent something from being","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"seen or expressed or from operating 抑制，忍住，压抑；查","exampleZh":"禁【考研大纲词汇】 The virus suppresses the body's immune system. 这种病毒 会抑制人体的免疫系统。 后缀：press按，压","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"compress","head":"v. /kəmˈpres/ (被)压紧（com- 共同，一起 + press","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"按，压）","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"depress","head":"v. /dɪˈpres/ 使沮丧（de- 离开，向下 + press 按，","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"压）","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"oppress","head":"v. /əˈpres/ 压迫（op- 逆，相反 + press 按，压）","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"pathogen","head":"n. /ˈpæθədʒən/ any small organism, such as a","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"virus or a bacterium that can cause disease 病原体【考研大","exampleZh":"纲词汇】 The spread of pathogens by insects. 病原体通过昆虫传播。","tags":[]},{"term":"serotonin","head":"n. /ˌserəˈtəʊnɪn/ a chemical in the brain that","definition":"affects how messages are sent from the brain to the body,","gloss":"","example":"and also affects how a person feels 血清素【考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"Serotonin—the happiness hormone. 血清素——快乐激素。 人体肠道中数以万亿计的微生物会将复杂碳水化合物消化 分解成脂肪酸，为人体提供约10%的热量。它们还能合成维生 素，尤其是维生素K（能够调节血液凝固）以及多种B族维生 素；帮助调节免疫系统；抑制病原体的生长；并调控血清素等 信号分子的生成，向大脑传递肠道信息也有这些信号分子的功 劳。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"tip-top","head":"adj. /ˈtɪp.tɒp/ excellent; perfect 非常优秀的，完美的","definition":"Even though our house is in tip-top condition, we're","gloss":"","example":"havingproblemssellingit.虽然我们的房子状况很好，但现在","exampleZh":"把它卖出去还是有困难。","tags":[]},{"term":"appetite","head":"n. /ˈæpɪtaɪt/ the feeling that you want to eat","definition":"","gloss":"food食欲，胃口【考研大纲词汇】","example":"Birds have different appetites for different types of insects.","exampleZh":"Both viruses cause fever and loss of appetite. 两种病毒都会 引起发烧以及食欲不振。 n. a strong desire for something 强烈欲望；渴望 不同鸟类对不同类型的昆虫有着不同的偏好。 因此，保持肠道微生物组处于最佳状态实属明智之举。人 们普遍认为，维持肠道内菌群多样化有助于保证微生物群的良 好状态。而且，由于不同菌种的口味各不相同，饮食种类丰富 也十分重要。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"ferment","head":"v. /fəˈment/ if food or drink ferments or if you","definition":"ferment it, it goes through a chemical change because of the action of yeast or bacteria, which may cause it to produce bubbles or heat, or turn sugars in it into alcohol.","gloss":"（使）发酵【考研大纲词汇】","example":"You make wine by leaving grape juice to ferment until all","exampleZh":"thesugarhasturnedtoalcohol.酿葡萄酒是让葡萄汁发酵， 直到所有的糖分都转化为酒精。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"off-the-peg","head":"adj. /ˌɒf.ðəˈpeɡ/ (US off-the-rack); (Australian","definition":"English off-the-hook) made and bought in standard sizes","gloss":"and not made especially to fit a particular person （衣服）","example":"She bought an off-the-peg suit because she couldn't","exampleZh":"均码的，标准码的；非定制的 affordatailoredone.她买了一套成品西装，因为她买不起定 制的。","tags":[]},{"term":"insufficient","head":"adj. /ˌɪnsəˈfɪʃnt/ not enough 不够的，不足的；不","definition":"","gloss":"充分的【考研大纲词汇】","example":"The funds available were insufficient to cover the cost of SYN inadequate, deficient ANT sufficient, adequate, ample","exampleZh":"theproject.可用的资金不足以支付该项目的费用。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"bespoke","head":"adj. /b ɪ ’sp ə ʊ k/ specially made for","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"a particular person 定做的；定制的","exampleZh":"He wears bespoke suits made by a tailor in Savile Row. 他 穿的是萨维尔街裁缝为他量身定制的西装。 2018年，一项由美国公众参与的科学研究项目显示，每周 食用30种植物食物的人，其肠道微生物组多样性明显高于每周 食用不足10种的人。斯坦福大学2021年发表的一项研究也证 实，泡菜、酸菜等发酵食品同样能够增加肠道微生物组的多样 性。不过，有些人觉得这种一刀切式的建议还不够。他们更希 望得到量身定制的方案。","tags":[]},{"term":"fistful","head":"n. /ˈfɪst.fʊl/ an amount of something that you can","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"hold in your fist 一把（之量）","exampleZh":"He held out a fistful of crumpled dollars. 他拿出一把皱巴巴 的钞票。","tags":[]},{"term":"so-called","head":"adj. /ˌsəʊ ˈkɔːld/ used to show that you think a","definition":"word that is used to describe sb/sth is not suitable or not","gloss":"correct 所谓的","example":"Her so-called friends never helped her when she was in adj. used to introduce a new word or phrase that is It isn't yet clear how dangerous these so-called \"super-","exampleZh":"trouble.她那些所谓的朋友在她遇到麻烦时从没帮过她。 not yet known by many people 叫做…的，名叫…的;所谓的 rats\"are.目前还不清楚这种名叫\"超级老鼠\"的东西有多危险。","tags":[]},{"term":"stool","head":"n. /stuːl/ a piece of solid waste from the body 粪便","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"He told the doctor he had been passing bloody stools. 他","exampleZh":"告诉医生他便血。","tags":[]},{"term":"compile","head":"v. /kəmˈpaɪl/ to collect information from","definition":"","gloss":"different places and arrange it in a book, report, or list 汇","example":"We're compiling some facts and figures for a documentary","exampleZh":"编；编纂；编辑；编制【考研大纲词汇】 onthesubject.我们正在为一部有关这个主题的纪录片汇编资 料。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"therein","head":"adv. /ˌðeərˈɪn/ in or into a particular place, thing,","definition":"","gloss":"etc.在那里;在其中;在那点上","example":"It is a thrilling tale of a haunted house and the ghosts","exampleZh":"therein.那是一个令人毛骨悚然的故事，讲的是一座凶宅还有里 面的幽灵。","tags":[]},{"term":"tailored","head":"adj. /ˈteɪləd/ (of clothes) made to fit a particular","definition":"","gloss":"personbyatailor（衣服）量身定制的，合身的","example":"SYN customized, personalized","exampleZh":"He wore a beautifully tailored suit to the wedding. 他穿了 一套剪裁精美的西装去参加婚礼。","tags":[]},{"term":"supplement","head":"n. /ˈsʌplɪmənt/ something that is added to","definition":"something else in order to improve it or complete it;","gloss":"somethingextra补充物，增补物【考研大纲词汇】","example":"Most doctors recommend taking vitamin supplements if v. /ˈsʌp.lɪ.ment/ to add something to something to make it Some vegetarians like to supplement their diets with iron.","exampleZh":"youarepregnant.大多数医生建议孕妇服用维生素补充剂。 largerorbetter增加，补充，增补 有些素食主义者喜欢在饮食之外吃一些含铁的药片。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"flag up phrasalverb to draw attention to sth 引起对…的注","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"意","example":"The report flagged up the dangers of under-age drinking.","exampleZh":"这篇报道引起大众对未成年人饮酒危害的关注。 只要花上一笔钱，他们就能得到这样的服务。所谓直接面 向消费者（D2C）的公司会分析粪便样本，根据其中检测到的 DNA和RNA，列出样本中所含微生物的清单。这类公司可能 还会提供个性化的饮食建议、活菌剂量以及专门有利于微生物 生长的补充剂，旨在填补检测所发现的微生物缺失。","tags":[]},{"term":"tinker","head":"v. /ˈtɪŋkə(r)/ to make small changes to something,","definition":"","gloss":"especially in an attempt to repair or improve it 修补；改","example":"I wish the government would stop tinkering with the healt","exampleZh":"进；摆弄 He spent the afternoon tinkering with his bicycle chain. 他 花了一下午摆弄他的自行车链条。 hservice.我希望政府不要再在公共医疗卫生服务上折腾了。","tags":[]},{"term":"scant","head":"adj. /skænt/ very little; not enough 很少的；不足的；","definition":"","gloss":"欠缺的","example":"The project received scant attention from the","exampleZh":"management.该项目没有得到管理层足够的关注。 adj.almost接近；差不多 Add a scant half litre of milk to the mixture and stir well. 把 接近半升的牛奶加入到混合物中，并搅拌均匀。","tags":[]},{"term":"proprietary","head":"adj. /prəˈpraɪətri/ (especially of information,","definition":"software, or a product) made and sold by a particular company and protected by a patent, trademark, or","gloss":"copyright from being copied or used by others （尤指信","example":"The company refuses to reveal the proprietary formula of","exampleZh":"这种方法的问题在于，可以作为参照标准的所谓“正确” 微生物组并不存在。事实上，不同人体内的微生物组可能存在 相当大的差异，却依然能够非常有效地为宿主带来理想的结 果。肠道健康不佳最明显的警讯，是生物多样性不足，而多样 化、且部分经过发酵的饮食恰恰有助于纠正这一问题。相比之 下，认为通过调整某一种微生物的存在与否，就能让健康状况 得到明显改善，这一观点几乎没有什么已发表的科学依据；而 且，许多D2C公司也不愿公开其相关主张所依据的专有数据的 具体细节。","tags":[]},{"term":"commerce","head":"n. /ˈkɒmɜːs/ the activity of buying and selling","definition":"","gloss":"goods and services, especially in large amounts; trade 商","example":"The new online platform has revolutionized cross-border","exampleZh":"业；贸易；（尤指大宗商品的）买卖【考研大纲词汇】 commerce.这个新的在线平台彻底改变了跨境贸易。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"respectable","head":"adj. /rɪˈspektəbl/ considered by society to be","definition":"acceptable, good, or of sufficient quality; deserving","gloss":"respectandapproval体面的；值得尊敬的；相当好的；可接","example":"The study was published in a respectable scientific journal.","exampleZh":"受的【考研大纲词汇】 该研究发表在一本相当权威的科学期刊上。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"respectful","head":"adj. /r ɪ ’spektfl/ showing admiration for","definition":"","gloss":"someoneorsomething毕恭毕敬的；表示尊敬的；尊重的","example":"“We're so pleased to meet you at last,” he said in a","exampleZh":"respectfultoneofvoice.“我们终于和您见面了，真是万分高 兴，”他毕恭毕敬地说道。 当然，也有例外。在英国，蒂姆·斯佩克特（Tim Spector）横跨学商两界，他在伦敦国王学院任职的同时，还参 与创办了一家名为Zoe的D2C公司。到目前为止，他在两个 身份之间来回切换，游刃有余。经客户许可，Zoe公司收集到 的用户数据会被纳入正规的同行评议研究。截至目前，这些研 究表明，个性化饮食并不会产生特别显著的效果，但或许能在 一些细微之处有所帮助。","tags":[]},{"term":"microbial","head":"adj. /maɪˈkrəʊbiəl/ relating to or caused by","definition":"microbes (= very small living things, especially bacteria,","gloss":"thatcancausedisease)微生物的；由微生物引起的","example":"The research focuses on the microbial communities living","exampleZh":"inthehumandigestivesystem.这项研究聚焦于生活在人类 消化系统中的微生物群落。","tags":[]},{"term":"census","head":"n. /ˈsensəs/ a count for official purposes, especially","definition":"one to count the number of people living in a country and","gloss":"to collect information about them （官方的）调查，统计;","example":"A national census is carried out every ten years in many","exampleZh":"（尤指）人口普查【考研大纲词汇】 countries.许多国家每十年进行一次全国人口普查。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"accurate","head":"adj. /ˈækjərət/ correct and true in every detail 准","definition":"","gloss":"确的；精确的；正确无误的【考研大纲词汇】","example":"The scientist needed accurate measurements to verify the ANT inaccurate, incorrect, approximate, vague","exampleZh":"experimentresults.这位科学家需要精确的测量数据来验证实 验结果。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"homogenise","head":"v. /həˈmɒdʒənaɪz/ to treat milk so that the","definition":"","gloss":"cream is mixed into other parts of the liquid 使均质（尤指","example":"The dairy industry homogenizes milk to prevent the cream v. to change something so that all its parts or features TV has homogenized the culture and language of large","exampleZh":"使牛奶中的油脂粒均匀分布） fromrising.乳制品行业将牛奶均质化，以防止油脂漂浮上升。 become the same or very similar （使）变均匀;（使）变纯 一;（使）变类同 partsoftheplanet.电视使地球上大部分地区的文化和语言同 质化。","tags":[]},{"term":"identical","head":"adj. /aɪˈdentɪkl/ exactly the same; not different in","definition":"","gloss":"anyway完全相同的；一模一样的【考研大纲词汇】","example":"The two samples produced almost identical results in the","exampleZh":"laboratorytest.这两个样本在实验室测试中得出了几乎完全相 同的结果。 不过，即便量身定制的方法确实有价值，它显然也必须建 立在D2C公司所进行的微生物普查足够准确的基础上。为了检 验这一点，美国国家标准与技术研究院的研究人员制备了21份 经过均质处理、因而完全相同的粪便样本，并给向7家D2C公 司每家寄出了3份。检测结果（已于2月发表）寄回后，人们 发现，不仅不同公司的分析结果之间存在明显差异，甚至有一 家公司的检测结果内部也有不同。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"put","head":"v. /pʊt/ to express or state something in a particular","definition":"","gloss":"way说；表达；表述","example":"To put it simply, the experiment failed because of human","exampleZh":"error.简单地说，实验失败是由于人为失误。","tags":[]},{"term":"bogus","head":"adj. /ˈbəʊɡəs/ (especially of a claim or a document)","definition":"","gloss":"not genuine; pretending to be real or true （尤指说法或文","example":"The insurance company suspected the claim was bogus (Para. 5) By contrast, the idea that tinkering with the presence or absence of this or that type of bug will perceptibly improve your health has scant published scientific basis, and many D2C firms are reluctant to share the details of proprietary data on which they base Para. 5 By contrast, the idea that tinkering with the presence or absence of this or that type of bug will perceptibly improve your health has scant published scientific basis, and many D2C firms are reluctant to share the details of By contrast, the idea that tinkering with the presence or absence of this or that type of bug will perceptibly improve your health has scant published scientific basis, and many D2C firms are reluctant to share the details of proprietary data on which they base their claims. do not have huge effects, but may help at the margins. or boundary of a group, place, or system, often used to describes people, ideas, or activities that have little power, Individually tailored diets may make a difference at the  yield modest gains idiom to produce small, limited, or average improvements, profits, or increases rather than The stock market recovery will yield modest gains for  move the needle idiomto make a noticeable, measurable value, it must surely depend on the microbial censuses carried out by D2C firms being accurate.  put something in place idiom to set up, establish, or implement a system, rule, plan, or physical object so it is  go through with something idiom to do a planned or promised action, especially when it is hard, scary, or you We have decided to go through with the original plan","exampleZh":"加州大学戴维斯分校的进化微生物学家乔纳森·艾森 （JonathanEisen）指出，微生物组存在差异，并不意味着个 性化微生物组医学时代就会很快到来。其实，他本人的话更为 直接：“（这个领域的）大多数说法都是骗人的。”所以，你 也许还是省下这笔钱，买罐泡菜更好。 August 15TH- 21ST ｜Science & technology 群公告学习流程精读， ase their claims. 相比之下，认 为通过调整某一种微生物的存在与否，就能让健康状况得到明显改 善，这一观点几乎没有什么已发表的科学依据；而且，许多D2C公 司也不愿公开其相关主张所依据的专有数据的具体细节。 主句1 伴随状语主语 同位语从句 主语 后置定语 程度状语谓语宾语 谓语宾语 主句2 主语系语表语 表语补足语 定语从句（修饰data） 地点状语主语谓语宾语 主句1： 伴随状语：Bycontrast；（bycontrast对比前文某种比较有科学 依据、看起来具有健康改善作用的观点/证据。而本句开始转向：作 者认为，通过调整微生物来改善健康缺乏科学依据。注意， however也可以用于对比，区别在于however表示转折，而by contrast表示“相比之下”，更强调比较两个对象之间的差异。） 主语：theidea； 同位语从句：（解释idea的内容。从句是主谓宾结构，已经是一个 完整的句子，that没有在里面充当任何成分，所以它不是定语从 句。） 引导词：that；主语：tinkering with the presence or absence； （tinkerwith不是简单的change，而是对某物进行小幅调整、改 动，带有“试着改改看”“随意调整”的意味。） 后置定语：of this or that type of bug；（this or that 在这里指 的不是前文已有内容，不表示“这个或那个”，而是表示“某一种 或另一种”，简言之就是“某种”。如Youcanchoosethisor thatoption.你可以选择某个选项。 the presence or absence （存在或不存在） of this or that type ofbug（某一种微生物的），字面意思是“某一种微生物的存在或 不存在”，太啰嗦。译文简化为“某一种微生物的存在与否”。） 程度状语：perceptibly；谓语：willimprove；宾语：your health；谓语：has；宾语：scant published scientific basis； 主句2： 连词：and；主语：manyD2Cfirms；系语：are；表语： reluctant；（and 并列两个分句，分句 1：the idea ... has scant published scientific basis ，分句 2 ： many D2C firms are reluctant to share...。这句话的结构就是[A has B], and [C are reluctant to D].） 表语补足语：to share the details of proprietary data； 定语从句（修饰data）： 地点状语：onwhich；主语：they；谓语：base；宾语：their claims；（their 指 many D2C firms） 写作积累 1. （Para. 6）So far, this suggests individually tailored diets at the margins 表示“being at the outer edge, border, influence, or involvement in the main part of society”，即 “只在有限程度上、在细微之处，仅带来边际性的”，例如， margin, even if their overall impact is limited. 即使个性化饮 食的总体影响有限，它在某些细微方面仍可能产生一定作用。此 外，还有以下表达可以表示类似的含义： large or dramatic breakthroughs 获得轻微的收益，收效不大 investorsthisyear.今年的股市复苏只会为投资者带来适度收 益。 difference or progress toward a goal 带来可感知的变化（与 atthemargins并不是完全同义，而是反向强调），产生足以 被注意到的变化 The treatment barely moves the needle. 这种治疗几乎没有 产生什么实质性改变。 2. （Para. 7）However, even if a bespoke approach does have Carry out 表示“to perform, complete, or execute a task, plan,order,orpromise”，即“实施、开展、进行（某项工作、 研究、调查、检测等）”，例如，Itishardtocarryoutthenew planinashorttime.在短时间内落实这个新计划很难。此外，还 有以下表达可以表示类似的含义： readytouse实施，使就位 The government put a new tax policy in place this year.政 府今年出台了一项新的税收政策。 feelunsureaboutit把…真正做下去，执行到底 despitethehighcost.尽管代价高昂，我们还是决定按原计划 把事情进行到底。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】8.23 检验题__阅读理解.docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, gut microbes help the body by _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"turning all of an individual's calories into fatty acids"},{"key":"B","text":"producing vitamins and helping regulate immune responses"},{"key":"C","text":"carrying serotonin messages from the brain to the gut"},{"key":"D","text":"eliminating pathogens through blood-clotting proteins"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·并列信息识别","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：The trillions of bugs in a human gut digest complex carbohydrates into fatty acids that provide about 10% of an individual's calories.","- 原文（Para.1）：They synthesise vitamins, notably K... They help tune the immune system. They suppress the growth of pathogens.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：过度推理陷阱。原文说脂肪酸提供约 10% 的热量，不是把全部热量都转化。","- 选项B（正确）：Para.1 明确说肠道微生物合成维生素，并帮助调节免疫系统。B 项将 synthesise vitamins 改写为 producing vitamins，把 help tune 改写为 helping regulate。","- 选项C（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文说血清素等信号分子参与从肠道向大脑发送信息，C 项把方向反转为从大脑到肠道。","- 选项D（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。微生物抑制病原体生长，维生素 K 参与凝血，但二者不是同一机制。","【命题技巧】","- 并列信息筛选：首段列出多种功能，正确项只保留原文明确支持的两项，避免跨句拼接。","- 比例与方向控制：A 的 all 和 C 的 brain to gut 都通过一个限定词改变原意。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"The phrase \"off-the-peg\" (Paragraph 3) most probably means _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"general and ready-made rather than tailored to a particular person"},{"key":"B","text":"expensive and therefore unavailable to ordinary consumers"},{"key":"C","text":"based on fermented foods and repeated weekly plant counts"},{"key":"D","text":"scientific but still waiting for publication in peer-reviewed journals"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】词义猜测题·短语语境义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3","【解析】","- 原文（Para.3）：Some people, though, feel such off-the-peg advice is insufficient. They would prefer something bespoke.","- 语境线索：off-the-peg 与 bespoke 形成对比；bespoke 在上下文中指“定制化”的方案。","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：off-the-peg 后文与 bespoke（定制的）相对，说明前者是通用型、现成建议，不针对个人。A 项准确利用反义关系解题。","- 选项B（错误）：无中生有陷阱。该短语强调建议形式，不涉及建议是否昂贵或普通人是否可获得。","- 选项C（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。植物数量和发酵食品是前文研究的具体内容，不是 off-the-peg 的词义。","- 选项D（错误）：偷换概念陷阱。文中研究来自 citizen-science project 和 Stanford University，但 off-the-peg 不表示“等待同行评审”。","【命题技巧】","- 对比线索：off-the-peg 与 bespoke 是解题核心：非定制 vs 定制。","- 熟词语境化：干扰项利用原文的 fermented、Stanford、published 等词，但都不是该短语的语境含义。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 5 that the author is sceptical of D2C microbiome services because _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"they cannot yet analyse stool samples through DNA and RNA technologies"},{"key":"B","text":"microbial diversity is unimportant to gut health and diet cannot correct it"},{"key":"C","text":"there is no single healthy microbiome reference and little published evidence for precise tailored benefits"},{"key":"D","text":"they refuse to obtain users' permission before feeding data into research"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】推理判断题·论证立场推理","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 5","【解析】","- 原文（Para.5）：The problem with this approach is that there is no “right” microbiome to act as a reference.","- 原文（Para.5）：By contrast, the idea that tinkering with the presence or absence of this or that type of bug will perceptibly improve your health has scant published scientific basis.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。Para.4 明确说 D2C 公司会基于粪便样本中的 DNA 和 RNA 分析微生物，因此技术上并非不能分析。","- 选项B（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文说缺乏生物多样性才是肠道健康不佳的最大红旗，多样饮食能改善这一点。","- 选项C（正确）：Para.5 指出没有统一的“正确”微生物组作为参照，而微调某种菌的进出会显著改善健康的说法缺乏充分发表证据。C 项概括了作者质疑的两个依据。","- 选项D（错误）：无中生有陷阱。Para.6 说 Zoe 在顾客许可下把结果用于研究，并没有说 D2C 公司普遍拒绝获得许可。","【命题技巧】","- 论点与论据对应：作者质疑的不是采样技术，而是“正常参照不存在”和“个性化干预证据不足”。","- 跨段干扰：A 来自 Para.4，D 来自 Para.6，均与 Para.5 的质疑理由不一致。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"The experiment with 21 sets of identical faeces is mentioned to show that _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"homogenising samples necessarily changes the microbes found in them"},{"key":"B","text":"seven D2C firms have agreed to standardise their testing methods"},{"key":"C","text":"one company's repeated errors explain all variation in microbiome science"},{"key":"D","text":"the same biological material may receive inconsistent reports from testing firms"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】例证题·实验证据功能","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 7","【解析】","- 原文（Para.7）：It must surely depend on the microbial censuses carried out by D2C firms being accurate.","- 原文（Para.7）：Researchers... prepared 21 sets of homogenised (and thus identical) faeces and sent three to each of seven D2C firms.","- 原文（Para.7）：There were notable differences not only between different firms' analyses but also, in one case, between those of an individual company.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：偷换概念陷阱。homogenised 的目的是让样本相同，原文没有说均质化必然改变样本中的微生物。","- 选项B（错误）：无中生有陷阱。七家公司参与检测，但原文没有说它们同意标准化检测方法。","- 选项C（错误）：过度推理陷阱。原文只说一家公司自身结果也不同，不能推出它解释了微生物组科学的全部差异。","- 选项D（正确）：实验把同一批均质化的相同粪便送给不同公司，却得到显著差异，甚至同一公司的结果也不一致。例子服务的是“检测准确性存疑”这一观点。","【命题技巧】","- 实验目的题：答案不是复述实验步骤，而是概括实验支持的结论：D2C 微生物检测可靠性不足。","- 极端词排除：C 项的 all variation 过度扩大单一公司案例的解释力。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Gut Bugs and Diet: Why Fermented Foods Beat Every Medical Treatment"},{"key":"B","text":"From Stool Sample to Supplement: The Rise of Reliable Personalised Nutrition"},{"key":"C","text":"Trillions of Bugs: How Serotonin Links Food to Brain Health"},{"key":"D","text":"Hacking the Gut? Strong Microbiome Claims, Thin Personalised Evidence"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·最佳标题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.3）：Some people, though, feel such off-the-peg advice is insufficient. They would prefer something bespoke.","- 原文（Para.5）：...there is no “right” microbiome to act as a reference... has scant published scientific basis.","- 原文（Para.8）：“Most of the claims [in this area] are bogus.” Perhaps better to save your money and invest in a jar of kimchi.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：过度推理陷阱。文章支持多样饮食和发酵食品，但没有说它们胜过一切医学治疗。","- 选项B（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。全文核心是质疑 D2C 个性化微生物组产品的证据和准确性，而不是宣告个性化营养已经可靠。","- 选项C（错误）：以偏概全陷阱。血清素只是首段列举的微生物功能之一，不是全文主线。","- 选项D（正确）：标题用问号回应“hack your gut microbiome”的诱惑，又用 strong claims, thin evidence 概括全文：肠道微生物重要，但商业化的个性化检测与干预缺乏坚实证据。","【命题技巧】","- 问号加评价：标题中的问号保留话题吸引力，后半句表明作者怀疑立场，避免只写关键词。","- 全文平衡：正确标题承认微生物组的重要性，同时突出对商业化检测的审慎批评。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】8.23检验题__完型填空.docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["The trillions of bugs in a human gut digest complex carbohydrates into fatty acids that provide about 10% of an individual’s calories. They ____【11】____ vitamins, notably K and various members of the B group. They help ____【12】____ the immune system. They ____【13】____ the growth of pathogens. And they ____【14】____ production of signalling molecules, such as serotonin, involved in sending messages from the gut to the brain.","Keeping your gut microbiome in tip-top condition is thus ____【15】____. Maintaining a diverse mix of bacteria in it is widely thought a good ____【16】____ to do this. And, since different species have different ____【17】____, diversity of diet makes sense.","In 2018 an American citizen-science project ____【18】____ that people eating 30 types of plants a week had significantly more diverse microbiomes than those eating fewer than ten. Work from Stanford University, published in 2021, ____【19】____ that fermented foods such as kimchi and sauerkraut diversify microbiomes, too. Some people, though, feel such off-the-peg advice is insufficient. They would prefer something bespoke, and D2C firms are happy to ____【20】____ it."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"consume"},{"key":"B","text":"synthesise"},{"key":"C","text":"destroy"},{"key":"D","text":"excrete"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (synthesise)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·生物学语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] consume（消耗）：肠道菌确实消耗物质，但本句强调生成维生素。语义场干扰。","[B] synthesise（合成）：They synthesise vitamins 表示肠道菌合成维生素。正确答案。","[C] destroy（破坏）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] excrete（排泄）：可通但语义不如合成精准。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ignore"},{"key":"B","text":"exhaust"},{"key":"C","text":"suppress"},{"key":"D","text":"tune"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (tune)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·动宾搭配","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第3句","【解析】","[A] ignore（忽视）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] exhaust（耗尽）：语义过强且方向相反。程度差异干扰。","[C] suppress（抑制）：抑制免疫系统与后文有益功能不符。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] tune（调节）：tune the immune system 表示调节免疫系统，比 control 更精确。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"suppress"},{"key":"B","text":"promote"},{"key":"C","text":"measure"},{"key":"D","text":"adjust"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (suppress)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·动宾搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第4句","【解析】","[A] suppress（抑制）：suppress the growth of pathogens（抑制病原体生长）是标准动宾搭配。正确答案。","[B] promote（促进）：与 pathogens（病原体）搭配后方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] measure（测量）：语义偏离，本句讲保护作用。语义场干扰。","[D] adjust（调整）：与 growth of pathogens 搭配语义不清。搭配干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"disrupt"},{"key":"B","text":"reduce"},{"key":"C","text":"regulate"},{"key":"D","text":"prevent"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (regulate)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·语义精确度","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第5句","【解析】","[A] disrupt（扰乱）：可搭配 production，但语义方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] reduce（减少）：语义过窄，不一定是减少。程度差异干扰。","[C] regulate（调节）：regulate production of signalling molecules 表示调节信号分子生成。正确答案。","[D] prevent（阻止）：语义过强。程度差异干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"optional"},{"key":"B","text":"useless"},{"key":"C","text":"risky"},{"key":"D","text":"wise"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (wise)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·作者态度","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] optional（可选的）：语气过弱，与 thus 推导不符。程度差异干扰。","[B] useless（无用的）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] risky（危险的）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] wise（明智的）：Keeping... is thus wise 承接上文有益功能。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reason"},{"key":"B","text":"goal"},{"key":"C","text":"way"},{"key":"D","text":"rule"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (way)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·上下文语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] reason（理由）：reason to do this 可通，但句意是“方法”。近义干扰。","[B] goal（目标）：Maintaining a diverse mix 已经是方法而非目标。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] way（方法）：a good way to do this（做这件事的好方法）与后文饮食多样性呼应。正确答案。","[D] rule（规则）：语义过强，后文只是普遍观点。程度差异干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"appetites"},{"key":"B","text":"sizes"},{"key":"C","text":"colours"},{"key":"D","text":"habitats"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (appetites)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·上下文语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第3句","【解析】","[A] appetites（食欲、营养偏好）：different species have different appetites 解释为何需要多样饮食。正确答案。","[B] sizes（大小）：语法可通，但与 diet diversity 无直接关系。语义场干扰。","[C] colours（颜色）：语义无关。语义场干扰。","[D] habitats（栖息地）：肠道菌群共享同一栖息地。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"showed"},{"key":"B","text":"denied"},{"key":"C","text":"doubted"},{"key":"D","text":"assumed"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (showed)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·研究结果","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] showed（表明）：project showed that... 是研究报告标准表达。正确答案。","[B] denied（否认）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] doubted（怀疑）：项目不是怀疑而是发现。语义场干扰。","[D] assumed（假定）：与 had significantly more diverse microbiomes 的数据结果不符。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"confirmed"},{"key":"B","text":"refuted"},{"key":"C","text":"ignored"},{"key":"D","text":"questioned"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (refuted)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·研究验证","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第2句","【解析】","[A] refuted（反驳）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] confirmed（证实）：Stanford 的研究证实发酵食品也能增加微生物组多样性。正确答案。","[C] ignored（忽视）：语义不通。语义场干扰。","[D] questioned（质疑）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sell"},{"key":"B","text":"ban"},{"key":"C","text":"delay"},{"key":"D","text":"provide"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (provide)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·动宾搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第4句","【解析】","[A] sell（售卖）：语法和局部语义可通，但不如 provide it 直接强调提供定制方案。近义干扰。","[B] ban（禁止）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] delay（延迟）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] provide（提供）：D2C firms are happy to provide it 指公司愿意提供定制建议。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"8.23 精读.pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":795309,"date":"2026-08-23","range":"","title":"Well Informed","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.23 精读.pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.23 检验题__阅读理解.docx","ext":".docx","bytes":55789,"date":"2026-08-23","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.23 检验题__阅读理解.docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.23检验题__完型填空.docx","ext":".docx","bytes":57787,"date":"2026-08-23","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.23检验题__完型填空.docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"layout","label":"杂志排版","file":"8.23杂志排版.pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":808888,"date":"2026-08-23","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.23杂志排版.pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
